2️⃣ Core idea (important)

We compute one derived score:

HLTV Reputation Score (0–100)

This score:

Is front-loaded toward the latest year

Decays older years aggressively

Is capped (no infinite stacking)

Can be cleanly removed after several seasons

3️⃣ Weighting model (this is the key)
Year decay curve (example)

You want something like this:

Year difference	Weight
Current year	1.00
−1 year	0.60
−2 years	0.35
−3 years	0.15
−4+ years	0.05

We’ll implement this with a function, not a table.

4️⃣ Rank → base value mapping

HLTV ranks are not linear. Top 3 matters way more than 15–20.

function rankToBaseValue(rank: number): number {
  if (rank <= 3) return 100;
  if (rank <= 5) return 90;
  if (rank <= 10) return 75;
  if (rank <= 15) return 60;
  return 45; // 16–20
}

5️⃣ Year decay function (clean + tunable)
function yearDecay(yearDiff: number): number {
  if (yearDiff <= 0) return 1;
  if (yearDiff === 1) return 0.6;
  if (yearDiff === 2) return 0.35;
  if (yearDiff === 3) return 0.15;
  return 0.05;
}


You can later replace this with an exponential if you want.

6️⃣ Final HLTV reputation score function

This is the main function you’ll call everywhere.

export function calculateHltvReputationScore(
  hltvHistory: HltvTop20Entry[] | undefined,
  currentYear: number
): number {
  if (!hltvHistory || hltvHistory.length === 0) {
    return 0;
  }

  let weightedSum = 0;
  let weightTotal = 0;

  for (const entry of hltvHistory) {
    const yearDiff = currentYear - entry.year;
    if (yearDiff < 0) continue; // future data not allowed

    const baseValue = rankToBaseValue(entry.rank);
    const weight = yearDecay(yearDiff);

    weightedSum += baseValue * weight;
    weightTotal += weight;
  }

  if (weightTotal === 0) return 0;

  // Normalize to 0–100
  const score = weightedSum / weightTotal;

  // Hard cap to prevent absurd legacy stacking
  return Math.min(Math.round(score), 100);
}

7️⃣ How this integrates into your systems
A) Reputation system (recommended)
player.worldReputation =
  baseReputation +
  calculateHltvReputationScore(player.hltvHistory, currentYear) * 0.4;


HLTV influences reputation

But does NOT dominate it

B) Transfer value modifier
transferValue =
  baseMarketValue *
  (1 + hltvScore / 200); // max +50%

C) AI behavior hooks (this is where it shines)
aiInterestScore += hltvScore * 0.3;
mediaAttention += hltvScore * 0.5;
fanExpectation += hltvScore * 0.4;


This makes AI:

chase ex-Top 5 players

overpay sometimes

generate drama naturally

8️⃣ IMPORTANT: seasonal decay in your sim

After each simulated season, you should do:

function decayHltvHistory(
  hltvHistory: HltvTop20Entry[],
  currentYear: number
): HltvTop20Entry[] {
  return hltvHistory.filter(entry => currentYear - entry.year <= 4);
}


After ~4–5 seasons:

HLTV influence ≈ gone

Your sim is fully autonomous

This is exactly what you want.

9️⃣ What NOT to do (seriously)

❌ Do not add HLTV score to match-day rating

❌ Do not let HLTV override role fit

❌ Do not keep HLTV forever

❌ Do not show “HLTV Rank” as sortable stat

